Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:27:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Paint the globe once for each eye of a stereo pair

MarbleMap::paintStereo() draws one world seen by two cameras around the
point of view. The globe is orthographic, so each camera orbits its
centre by half of the separation (the planet's axis turned about the
vertical axis), not toe-in. The stars are at infinity and take the
globe's maximum parallax instead of turning with it. The interface
layers are painted once, with the point of view, over both views.

LayerManager::renderLayers() takes the group of render positions to
paint (sky, globe, interface), all of them by default, and
TextureLayer repaints when only the planet's axis changed.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
