+    /**
+     * @brief Paint the map as a stereo pair: one world seen by two cameras around the point of view.
+     *
+     * The sky and the globe are painted once for each eye, with that eye's camera: an orthographic globe has no perspective
+     * to take off-axis cameras from, so each camera orbits the globe's centre by half of the separation (the planet's axis
+     * turned about the vertical axis), the left one so that the near side of the globe moves to the right. The stars are
+     * at infinity: they do not turn with the globe but take its maximum parallax, that of its far side. The interface
+     * (popups, float items, tools) is painted once, with the point of view, so it is the same in both eyes.
+     * @param leftEye painter of the left eye's view
+     * @param rightEye painter of the right eye's view, of the same size
+     * @param painter painter of the interface, of the same size, over both views
+     * @param separation angle between the two cameras, in radians
+     */
+    void paintStereo(GeoPainter &leftEye, GeoPainter &rightEye, GeoPainter &painter, qreal separation);
+
 public Q_SLOTS:
 
